  "unresolved": [
    "Every station in this county that publishes sky is an airport METAR, and airports sit inland of the beaches they are bound to. Sky and visibility therefore describe the airport and not the shoreline, and the distance is recorded per beach and shown to the reader rather than hidden.",
    "METAR stops at ten statute miles. The stations publish that ceiling as either 16093.44 m or 16090 m depending on the station, so a reading at the top of the range means \"at least ten miles\" and never \"exactly ten miles\". It is rendered as \"10 miles or more\" for that reason.",
    "A capability here means \"published at least once in 6 observations\", so a station that publishes a field rarely sits close to flipping. KF70 carried sky on one observation of six and is the row most likely to move a future --check; no beach binds it, so nothing a reader sees turns on it. The threshold is not raised to keep the check quiet, because a station that publishes sky once in six genuinely does publish sky.",
    "The shore classification is an author judgement, written by hand because no upstream authority publishes one. It has not been checked against a marine-layer study, and the case it most affects is San Diego Bay, where a station at sea level sits behind a 130 m peninsula from the ocean beaches it serves."
  ]
